libzint
-------

The encoders, the vector geometry, the SVG writer, the GS1 reduction, the ECI
conversion, the Reed-Solomon code, and the float32 narrowing are a behavioral
port of libzint from zint 2.16.0 (https://github.com/zint/zint,
https://zint.org.uk). libzint is Copyright (C) 2008-2025 Robin Stuart
<rstuart114@gmail.com> and contributors, and is licensed under the
BSD-3-Clause license. A copy is in vendor/zint/LICENSE. The conditions that
matter here:

1. Redistributions of source code must retain the copyright notice, the
   conditions, and the disclaimer.
2. Redistributions in binary form must reproduce them in the documentation
   or other materials provided with the distribution.
3. Neither the name of the project nor the names of its contributors may be
   used to endorse or promote products derived from this software without
   specific prior written permission.

This project is not affiliated with the zint project, and the names of Robin
Stuart and the zint project are not an endorsement of lua-zint-svg.

vendor/zint is the upstream tree, kept so the remaining symbologies can be
read from it and so SVG output can be compared against that release. It is
not part of the Lua rock. The libzint backend in that tree is BSD-3-Clause.
The command-line program and the Qt front end are GPL-3.0-or-later. Their
license files stay next to that source.

Option parser
-------------

src/zint/options.lua is MIT. It was written from the zint 2.16.0 manual and
from byte comparison against the pinned command-line program. It is not a
clean-room file: an earlier transcription of the GPL-3 frontend/main.c option
parser was read while the port was being built. That transcription is not in
this repository.

